{"title":"Career Roadmap · Construction Manager","role":"Construction Manager","summary":"A Construction Manager plans, coordinates, and controls construction projects from pre-construction through completion. The role combines civil/construction engineering, project planning, cost control, contracts, quality, safety, procurement, scheduling, and team management.","facts":{},"about":[{"label":"Important","text":"Construction Manager is generally a mid-career role, not a typical first job after graduation. A realistic progression is Graduate Engineer → Site/Planning/Project Engineer → Senior Engineer → Construction Manager."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Typical career stage","Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Graduate / Junior Engineer"},{"text":"Site execution, estimation, planning, QA/QC"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Site / Planning / Project Engineer"},{"text":"Sections/work packages, contractors, schedules, cost"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Senior Project / Construction Engineer"},{"text":"Multiple work packages, teams, budgets, contracts"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Construction Manager / Project Manager"},{"text":"End-to-end project delivery and leadership"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Main objective","Key skills","Proof of progress"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Engineering foundation"},{"text":"Construction materials, mechanics, surveying, drawings, Excel"},{"text":"Building planning exercise"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Construction systems"},{"text":"RCC, steel, geotechnical, estimation, construction methods"},{"text":"BOQ + cost-estimation project"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Project management foundation"},{"text":"Planning, Primavera, contracts, QA/QC, safety, BIM"},{"text":"Construction internship"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Management readiness"},{"text":"Scheduling, cost control, risk, procurement, contracts, BIM"},{"text":"Complete construction management capstone"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Engineering & construction foundation"},{"type":"h","text":"Core subjects"},{"type":"p","text":"Build a strong foundation in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Engineering Mathematics"},{"text":"Engineering Mechanics"},{"text":"Strength of Materials"},{"text":"Engineering Drawing"},{"text":"Building Materials"},{"text":"Surveying"},{"text":"Basic Structural Engineering"},{"text":"Basic Construction Technology"},{"text":"Introduction to Project Management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technical tools"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AutoCAD"},{"text":"MS Excel"},{"text":"Basic quantity calculations"},{"text":"Basic surveying"},{"text":"Engineering drawings"},{"text":"Construction documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Practical project"},{"type":"h","text":"G+2 Residential Building Planning"},{"type":"p","text":"Prepare:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Site plan"},{"text":"Floor plans"},{"text":"Elevations"},{"text":"Sections"},{"text":"Area calculations"},{"text":"Preliminary material quantities"},{"text":"Construction sequence"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Gap moved","text":"Engineering theory → understanding the construction lifecycle."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Construction engineering"},{"type":"p","text":"Now move from basic engineering into actual construction systems."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"RCC construction"},{"text":"Steel construction"},{"text":"Masonry"},{"text":"Concrete technology"},{"text":"Foundation construction"},{"text":"Geotechnical engineering"},{"text":"Building services"},{"text":"Construction equipment"},{"text":"Road construction"},{"text":"Water and infrastructure construction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Construction sequence"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Site preparation","excavation",